  "Question": "At Clover View Junior High, one half of the students go home on the school bus. One fourth go home by automobile. One tenth go home on their bicycles. The rest walk home. What fractional part of the students walk home?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{16}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac{3}{20}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac13\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{17}{20}\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac{9}{10}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "All the students together represent \\(1\\). Since the walking students are the remaining group, subtract the bus, automobile, and bicycle fractions from \\(1\\). Using twentieths gives\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n1-\\left(\\frac12+\\frac14+\\frac1{10}\\right)\n&=\\frac{20}{20}-\\left(\\frac{10}{20}+\\frac5{20}+\\frac2{20}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\frac3{20}.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nTherefore \\(\\frac3{20}\\) of the students walk home, choice B.",
